abstract: >-
  Maple worksheets, Julia solvers and computed spectra for the quasinormal modes of a massless scalar field around
  four-dimensional Schwarzschild–anti-de Sitter black holes, with the vanishing-field condition at the AdS boundary and
  with a one-parameter relation between the two coefficients of the field at large radius, studied as a formal
  deformation. A Chebyshev collocation turns the radial problem into a quadratic matrix pencil, assembled with 200
  decimal digits and solved with 220 digits at three resolutions, and only the roots on which they agree are kept;
  48 tables of modes are included.
